<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on limited markets.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on limited markets.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean was firm in central Indian markets on limited arrivals on Thursday with prices up by 100-150 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Traders are creating stocks to get a better price, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell on increased selling from soybean proccessing plants and selling from soybean processing plants and refineries. Soyoil prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Business volume was dull and the undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Dealers said soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained weak in thin trade. Export demand was dull against increased selling. Soymeal yellow was $270 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $135-136 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. The undertone was weak.</p>
